/**
 * Washington Real Estate Practices (30 clock hours) — module question bank.
 *
 * THE SECOND OF THE TWO COURSES RCW 18.85.101(1)(c) NAMES. With Real Estate Fundamentals (60 clock hours)
 * it delivers the statutory 90 hours exactly. The statute names both courses and ALLOCATES HOURS TO
 * NEITHER; the 60/30 split is a StateCourse proposal requiring Department confirmation, and WAC
 * 308-124H-810 requires an approved school to use the Department's own prescribed curriculum, which this
 * project did not obtain.
 *
 * THE SENTENCE THIS COURSE IS BUILT ON. RCW 18.86.110: "The duties under this chapter are STATUTORY DUTIES
 * AND NOT FIDUCIARY DUTIES. This chapter SUPERSEDES THE FIDUCIARY DUTIES of an agent to a principal under
 * the common law. The common law continues to apply to the parties in all other respects. This chapter does
 * not affect the duties of a broker while engaging in the authorized or unauthorized practice of law as
 * determined by the courts of this state. This chapter shall be construed broadly."
 *
 * Washington KEPT THE WORD "AGENT" AND REPLACED WHAT STANDS BEHIND IT. No item in this bank may present a
 * common-law fiduciary duty as Washington law, and several items exist specifically to catch a student who
 * arrived with a national textbook's account. What remains is the list in RCW 18.86.030, owed to ALL
 * PARTIES and UNWAIVABLE, plus the relationship lists in .040, .050 and .060 — and nothing else.
 *
 * THREE PROVISIONS THAT REVERSE WHAT A STUDENT EXPECTS:
 *   RCW 18.86.030(1)(c) — present all written offers "REGARDLESS OF whether the property is subject to an
 *                         existing contract for sale." Many states soften this duty; Washington does not,
 *                         and it sits inside a paragraph saying the duties may not be waived.
 *   RCW 18.86.100      — a principal does NOT have knowledge or notice of facts known by an agent that the
 *                         principal does not actually know. The common law imputes; Washington does not.
 *   RCW 18.86.090      — a principal is generally NOT liable for an agent's acts, with two narrow exits.
 *
 * WASHINGTON LICENSES A BROKER, NOT A SALESPERSON. RCW 18.86.010(3). No item may refer to a Washington
 * "salesperson."
 *
 * THE EXAMINATION THIS COURSE MUST CARRY. WAC 308-124H-820(8): a course of 30 clock hours or more needs a
 * comprehensive examination of no fewer than three questions per clock hour with a minimum of 90 questions,
 * and a passing course grade of AT LEAST 70 PERCENT. At 30 clock hours that is A MINIMUM OF 90 ITEMS. The
 * 70 percent is the DIRECTOR'S figure. The items here are NOT that examination — they gate progression and
 * are visible by design, and the 80 percent engagement threshold is a StateCourse standard.
 *
 * Each module carries one applied item, five engagement items and five remediation items. The correct
 * answer is authored at index 0 and permuted deterministically per item id at delivery. The public delivery
 * path strips correctChoice and rationale, and a test proves it.
 *
 * WHAT WAS NOT OBTAINED, AND WHICH THEREFORE APPEARS IN NO ITEM: the Department's prescribed curriculum;
 * THE FULL TEXT OF THE RCW 18.86.120 PAMPHLET; the remainder of RCW 18.85 including RCW 18.85.011 and
 * 18.85.361; WAC 308-124 and its trust account, advertising and record-retention rules; RCW 64.06 and the
 * seller disclosure statement; RCW 59.18; RCW 49.60 and the federal Fair Housing Act; RCW 82.45; and
 * RESPA, TILA and TRID. No item asks a student to recall or reproduce anything from any of them, and every
 * rate in every item is supplied inside the item as a given.
 *
 * Course version 1.0 submission draft — NOT APPROVED. No Washington clock hours are available.
 */

